# This project's environment.
#
# `zen run` reads this file before it loads the project, and forwards every
# name in it into the sandbox — so a command the agent runs sees the same
# variables the run does. Values are forwarded by name, never written onto a
# command line, and `--no-keys` withholds the whole file.
#
# Precedence: what is already set in your shell wins, then this file, then the
# keyring (`zen key add`). So this is the place for what belongs to *this*
# project — the credential one of its tools needs, the address of the service
# it talks to — and the keyring is the place for what belongs to you.
#
# It is in .gitignore, and should stay there. Everything else in the project is
# meant to be read, copied and shared; this is the one file that is not.
#
# A credential *file* — GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS — may be named by a path
# relative to this directory. It is mounted into the sandbox where the agent
# can read it, which is worth knowing before you point at one.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ACME_API_TOKEN=
# ACME_BASE_URL=https://api.example.test
